Android's active track window reaches two rows further. cRSubGame::AI (00082214) scans
rows up to the window's trailing edge plus 48, not 46, and up to 40 rows past the finish
line, not 20. cRSubGoldy::AI (0007ac54) keeps the trailing edge at the snail's z - 8 to
30 rows past the finish line, where Windows stops it 30 rows before the line, and
cRSubGoldy::Init (00079da8) starts it at -3, not -19. The other 46-row reaches ahead of
the snail grow to 48 with it: the finish banner shows within them (cRBanner::AI,
0006da24), salt fades in across them (cRSalt::AI, 00072318) and a shot retires beyond
them (cRSubGolb::AI, 000635d4). That function also lets a WALL2 cell stop a shot only
between heights -1 and 7.

